-- title:
--   Drinfeld's deformation ring of a special formal mathcal O_D-module
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a commutative domain $Onr$ which is a discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero and a $\mathbb Z_q$-algebra, such that $Onr$ is adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $q$, that ideal is maximal, and the residue field $k$ of $Onr$ is algebraically closed. Let $\iota : W(\mathbb F_{q^2}) \to Onr$ be a ring homomorphism (writing `Zp2 q` for the Witt vectors of the field with $q^2$ elements) and let $X_0$ be a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module over $k$ for the reduction $\mathrm{res}\circ\iota$ — that is, a commutative $2$-dimensional formal group law with an action of $W(\mathbb F_{q^2})$ by endomorphisms and a further endomorphism $\varpi$ with $\varpi\circ\varpi = [q]$ and $\varpi\circ[a] = [\sigma a]\circ\varpi$ — which is special (the Lie algebra is the direct sum of its two weight pieces `lieZero`, `lieOne`, each an invertible module) and of height $4$ (the endomorphism $[q]$ has kernel of degree $q^4$). Then there are a regular local $Onr$-algebra $R$, complete for its maximal-ideal-adic topology, a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{res}_R : R \to k$ extending the residue map of $Onr$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\mathcal X$ over $R$ and an isomorphism $w_u : \mathcal X \otimes_{\mathrm{res}_R} k \to X_0$ of formal $\mathcal O_D$-modules such that: for every Artinian local $Onr$-algebra $A$ with surjection $\mathrm{res}_A : A \to k$ extending the residue map of $Onr$, every formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X$ over $A$ which is special for $\iota$ and of height $4$, and every isomorphism $w : X\otimes_{\mathrm{res}_A} k \to X_0$, there is exactly one $Onr$-algebra homomorphism $\chi : R \to A$ with $\mathrm{res}_A\circ\chi = \mathrm{res}_R$ admitting an isomorphism $v : \mathcal X\otimes_\chi A \to X$ whose reduction satisfies $w\circ (v\otimes k) = w_u$ on power series; moreover the image of $q$ in $R$ is nonzero and $R$ is isomorphic, as an $Onr$-algebra, either to $Onr[[t]]$ or to [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel Onr q`](def/ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel.html#L15), the quotient of the two-variable power series ring over $Onr$ by `uvCrossingIdeal`.
--
--   This is Drinfeld's determination of the formal moduli of a special formal $\mathcal O_D$-module of height $4$ over an algebraically closed field of characteristic $q$: the deformation functor is pro-represented by a complete regular local ring which is either a one-variable power series ring or a crossing model, matching the complete local rings of the formal model of the $q$-adic upper half plane at smooth points and at ordinary double points of the special fibre. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation, where it supplies the regular pro-representing local ring attached to a closed point of the relevant fine moduli problem.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_SpecialFormalODModule_exists_isProrepresentedBy_deformations_powerSeries_or_uvCrossingModel.lean

